    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29378" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσπειθ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hard to persuade, not
				easily talked over</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				271d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>self-willed, disobedient</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				880a
			</span></i>, Hierocl.<i><span class="en">
				p.63A.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					4.1.3
				</span></i>
			 (
				Sup.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>hard to believe</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>D.</u>
				3.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῶς, ἔχειν πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Galb.</u>
					25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. φέρειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					15
				</span></i>
			; <i>with difficulty</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάμπτεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hero
					<u>Bel.</u>
					75.9
				</span></i>
			.</div>
